      "sequence_position": 16,
      "problem": "Let $[\\,i\\,]_{223}$ denote the residue class modulo $223$ containing the element $i\\in Z.$ Select the correct options in the statements below.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}={[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following properties:\n\n- ${⋃}_{i=0}^{222}\\,[\\,i\\,]_{223}=Z$\n\n- $[\\,21\\,]_{223}\\cap [\\,162\\,]_{223}=∅$\n\n- ${Z}_{223}={[\\,i\\,]_{223}\\,∣\\,0\\le i<223}$",
